  "slug": "rice-adventitious-2660",
  "summary": "New work links transcription factor modules and regulatory variants to xylem wall patterning, rice root and panicle architecture, and drought and salt tolerance.",
  "synthesis": "The items share a focus on discrete regulatory modules that set organ morphology and physiological performance, mostly in rice and other grasses. A single-cell xylem atlas identifies ZHD3 and ZHD4 as central regulators of protoxylem secondary cell wall morphology. In rice, OsWOX11 promotes thick AR2 adventitious roots, and a promoter variant (Hap3) shows higher activity. CArG-box deletions near APO1 quantitatively increase panicle secondary branching, pointing to recurrent cis-regulatory change. RLC3 pairs with KNOX proteins to activate lignin genes, controlling leaf rolling and drought tolerance. In creeping bentgrass, dosage-sensitive miR164-NAC tuning separates growth, drought and salt responses via AsNHX1. Together, these studies emphasize quantitative regulatory variation and secondary wall programs as levers on architecture and stress tolerance.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
